-- title:
--   Finite surjective morphism of two-chart models over the Γ₀(p) floor
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ and $K_1$ be intermediate fields of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ with $K_1 \le K$, where $K$ is the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and $K_1$ the one generated by that of $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $A$-algebra structures on $K$ and $K_1$ compatible with $L$, let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $j \in K$, $j_1 \in K_1$ be nonzero elements whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $j(q)$. Writing $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ and $\mathrm{chartAlgInf}$ for the subalgebras of elements integral over $A[j]$ and over $A[j^{-1}]$ respectively, and $\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}$ for the scheme obtained by gluing the spectra of these two chart algebras along the middle chart, the assertion is that there exist a morphism $m$ from the model of $(K,j)$ to the model of $(K_1,j_1)$ and $A$-algebra maps $\iota_F$, $\iota_I$ between the corresponding finite and infinite chart algebras such that: $\iota_F$ and $\iota_I$ are compatible with the inclusion $K_1 \subseteq K$ on underlying Laurent series; $m$ followed by the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ of the target model is the structure morphism of the source; the two squares comparing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\iota_F$, of $\iota_I$ with the canonical chart immersions and $m$ commute; $m$ pulls back the open range of each chart immersion of the target to the corresponding open range in the source; $m$ is finite with surjective underlying map; $\iota_F$ and $\iota_I$ are module-finite ring maps; and an element of $K$ lies in $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ (respectively $\mathrm{chartAlgInf}\,A\,K\,j$) exactly when it is integral over the image of $\iota_F$ (respectively $\iota_I$) inside that chart algebra.
--
--   This is the functoriality of the two-chart integral model along the inclusion of function fields $K_1 \subseteq K$ corresponding to the degeneracy map from $X_1(Mp)$ to the $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$ floor, together with the identification of the chart algebras upstairs as the integral closures of the images of the chart algebras downstairs. It is used in the analysis of the local structure of the model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A$ at supersingular points, where the completed local ring is computed from the floor, and in the statement that the finite chart is unramified away from the relevant maximal ideals.
